                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">INDOOR THERMAL COMFORT
Buoyant stratification + a comfort verdict.
Units: METERS. Temperatures in Celsius.

ROOM 6 x 4 x 3 m, cell size 0.3 m.
Inlet 1 m2 LOW on x=0 (z 0.3-1.3) at 0.1 m/s.
Outlet HIGH on x=6 (z 2.7-3.0). Low-in / high-out
is what lets the buoyant plume leave the room.

HEAT SOURCE zone (2.5,1.5,0.2)-(3.5,2.5,0.8),
3000 W. A heat source switches Indoor Case to the
buoyant fluid solver, so warm air rises and the
ceiling reads warmer than the floor.
From TestIndoorHotRoomContainerE2E.

WALL BANDS from TestIndoorWallPatchContainerE2E:
hotWall  = upper band of x=0, z 2-3, 40 C
coldWall = lower band of x=6, z 0-1, 10 C
Room faces not covered keep the case-wide Wall
Temp, which is left unset here.

TWO-NODE COMFORT ships at its own defaults with
Air Speed set to the 0.1 m/s inlet. Air and
radiant temperature must come from the solved
field - nothing on this canvas can supply them
before you run the case.

DEVIATION: the fixture's outlet rectangle starts
at z 2.7 and runs 1 m, i.e. 0.7 m THROUGH the
ceiling; only z 2.7-3.0 ever meshes. This template
draws that meshed part, so no surface sits outside
the room.

KNOWN WARNING: the heat zone is 0.6 m at its
thinnest against the 1.2 m background cell.

Action toggles ship OFF.</item>
                  </items>
